0.0.1
    * setup the main files for the app
    * fill in the simple counter logic for the button in the top bar
    * add stylesheet for counter indicator and its text label
0.0.2
    * add settings for the task list window width
0.0.3
    * implement dynamical response to settings changes without enable/disable
0.0.4
    * remove unnecessary style fields
    * remove button increase/decrease logic
    * add task item list and enter text box
0.0.5
    * put the cursor into the text entry box automatically after a click on the counter
0.0.6
    * implement task addition and editting features
0.0.7
    * switch from button release to button press triggers in task edit method
    * add task completed/delete button
    * make the delete button appear only when mouse hovers over the task
0.0.8
    * introduce more abstraction for task container and organize the code accordingly
    * add error handling for settings
    * add editing-entry style to highlight the current task entry being edited
0.0.9
    * add task persistence to save/load tasks from storage file for GNOME Shell restart or disabled extension
    * add settings to enable/disable task persistence
    * delete saved tasks when task persistence is disabled
0.1.0
    * add task preview feature expecially for long note takers
    * add enable/disable and customization for task preview feature
    * refactor prefs.js file for better code reusability
0.1.1
    * refactor taskContainer object for better signal handling and hand-off
    * switch from reactive textLabel to reactive taskContainer
    * tweak css file parameters to remove twitches in task editing
0.2.0
    * port extension.js and prefs.js to the ES module / class-based extension API required by GNOME Shell 45+
    * drop imports.misc.extensionUtils and imports.byteArray in favor of the Extension/ExtensionPreferences base classes and TextDecoder
    * rewrite prefs.js with Adw.PreferencesPage/SwitchRow/SpinRow and settings.bind(), replacing the manual Gtk widget wiring
    * clean up the task preview popup actor on disable() to avoid leaking chrome across enable/disable cycles
    * bump shell-version to 45-49; drop support for GNOME 3.36-43, which cannot load ESM extensions
0.2.1
    * add GNOME Shell 50 to shell-version after testing the port live in a GNOME 50 VM
    * fix prefs.js's resource import path (the Extensions app resolves its bundled
      modules under resource:///org/gnome/Shell/Extensions/js/..., not the
      lowercase path extension.js uses inside the Shell process)
0.2.2
    * track tasks in an explicit ordered list instead of introspecting the task
      list's DOM structure in _saveTasks(); also fixes a task being silently
      dropped from persisted storage if a save happens to run while it's
      mid-edit
    * fix the double-click reset timer leaking past task deletion by tracking
      and cancelling it in destroy(); read the reset delay from the desktop's
      configured double-click time instead of a hardcoded 500ms
    * guard the deferred idle_add callbacks in TaskContainer against a
      destroy-in-flight race, and cancel any still-pending ones in destroy()
    * create the extension's data directory before writing savedTasks.json,
      instead of silently failing to persist on a fresh profile
    * fix dead error handling around enable()'s settings fetch: getSettings()
      throws rather than returning a falsy value on failure
0.2.3
    * fix _deleteTask() bypassing TaskContainer's own destroy(): calling
      getContainer().destroy() directly skipped signal disconnection and
      pending-timeout/idle cleanup, and destroyed the delete button
      synchronously from inside its own 'clicked' handler, surfacing as
      "already disposed" warnings when deleting a task while another was
      mid-edit
    * fix a crash in _handleFocusLoss on any button-press with no resolvable
      source actor (e.g. a click on bare stage background) while a task was
      being edited
    * fix the delete button staying visible on a task after editing it,
      caused by nothing resetting its hover state when it's pulled out of
      the list for editing
    * rework hover tracking to be driven by motion events on the whole task
      list instead of each row's own enter/leave-event: under fast hovering,
      Clutter's per-row crossing detection can skip firing leave-event for a
      row swept past quickly, permanently sticking its delete button visible
    * clear savedTasks.json immediately when persist-tasks is turned off in
      prefs, instead of waiting for the next enable() (next logout/login)
0.3.0
    * add drag-and-drop task reordering: press and drag a task's text to move
      it, with a drop-line indicator showing where it would land; the order
      and persisted storage only update on release
    * distinguish a drag from a click/double-click using the desktop's
      configured drag threshold (dnd_drag_threshold), mirroring the
      double-click-time approach already used for click detection
    * detect the drag gesture and track it while in progress by polling the
      live pointer/button state rather than motion-event/button-release-event,
      after testing showed those events can be buffered/delayed while a
      mouse button is held down in some environments
    * an in-progress drag is force-cancelled (with nothing reordered or
      saved) if the popup menu closes for any reason mid-drag, or the
      extension is disabled, so no stray listener or timer is left running
0.3.1
    * fix the indicator's task counter surviving a disable/enable cycle with
      persistence off: it's a plain instance field that isn't re-created on
      a toggle, and neither disable() nor _loadTasks()'s persist-off branch
      reset it, so the label kept showing the old count against an emptied
      list
    * fix the task list shifting when entering edit mode: the row and the
      edit entry don't naturally compute to the same height from their CSS,
      so swapping between them moved every row below by the difference; the
      entry is now pinned to the row's actual measured height
    * restyle the drag-and-drop drop indicator: from a fully-opaque accent
      blue (which borrowed a color otherwise meaning "editing") to a thin,
      translucent white/gray line, tying it instead to the existing row
      separator color
    * trim comment density throughout extension.js (no functional changes)
0.3.2
    * add a GPL-2.0-or-later LICENSE, license headers on extension.js/prefs.js,
      and a fuller README (features, install instructions, credits to the
      original macOS Jinni app by Dino Angelov, license)
    * fix turning persist-tasks on not saving the current in-memory task list:
      only the "turn off" direction cleared the file instantly: turning it
      back on did nothing until the next add/edit/delete, losing tasks added
      while persistence was off if the session ended before that happened
0.3.3
    * checked the extension against the official EGO review guidelines
      (gjs.guide/extensions/review-guidelines); found and fixed two real gaps:
      disable() wasn't destroying live TaskContainer instances, so a pending
      hover/click-reset/drag-threshold timer could survive disable() and
      later fire against a disposed actor; and the temporary edit St.Entry
      was only ever unparented, never destroy()'d, left to JS garbage
      collection instead of releasing its native actor resources
    * split TaskContainer.destroy() into cancelPendingWork() (signals/timers
      only) plus the existing deferred widget destruction, and had disable()
      call the former: calling full destroy() per task there raced against
      the indicator's own synchronous destroy() cascade, which flooded the
      log with "already disposed" warnings once the deferred per-task widget
      destruction ran on top of an already-torn-down actor tree
0.3.4
    * trim comment density again (no functional changes)
    * fix a spurious "Failed to load tasks from file" error logged on every
      first run (or any run with no savedTasks.json yet): check for the
      file's existence first instead of letting GLib.file_get_contents()
      throw on a missing file and logging that as a failure
0.4.0
    * address all 5 warnings from extensions.gnome.org's Shexli static
      analyzer:
      - switched _saveTasks()/_loadTasks() from sync file I/O
        (GLib.file_get_contents()/Gio.File.replace_contents()) to their
        async counterparts, since shell code shouldn't block on file I/O;
        the load path is cancelled in disable()
      - consolidated the file-I/O error logging into one _logFileError()
        helper, dropping the console.error call-site count under the
        excessive-logging threshold
      - _entry, _label, _listBox, and TaskPreview's _popupLabel are now
        explicitly destroyed (and their signal handlers explicitly
        disconnected) in disable(), rather than relying only on the
        indicator's destroy() cascade
      - the deferred idle_add in _saveCurrentEntry() that destroys the old
        edit entry is now tracked on the instance instead of a bare local,
        so disable() can cancel/finish it if it runs first
    * fix: the async replace_contents_async() needs a GLib.Bytes, not a raw
      string like the sync version accepted
0.4.1
    * fix a task landing in the wrong list position after deleting other
      tasks earlier in the list while it was still being edited:
      _editTask() captured the entry's position once when editing started,
      and _listBox's children shift as earlier tasks get deleted, but that
      captured index was never updated to match. Recompute the entry's
      actual position at save time instead of trusting the stale one, and
      drop the now-unnecessary _currentIndex field entirely